& [SelectedPurpose] is one pure supplied-set assembler
  + retain one root carrier and every supplied descendant carrier without downgrade
  + reapply current M2A validation to the supplied limits and every projected entry
  + require exact identity, reference, path, volume, ordinal, limit, and ancestor relationships inside the supplied set
  + order descendants by one explicit structural comparator without changing their ordinals
  + derive checked entry count and total regular-file byte count
  + release one output-only wrapper containing the complete ordered carrier sequence
  - never: accept raw TopologyEntryObservation, lower evidence fragments, or caller-declared success
  - never: calculate an aggregate digest or construct a TopologyReceipt
  - never: perform or imply physical observation

& [WhyThisSlice] is dependency ordered
  + root, descendant-directory, and regular-file output-only carrier families are complete and proven
  + mixed set checks can now retain complete lower lineage rather than collapsing to public deserializable M2A forms
  + duplicate, volume, parent, order, ordinal, and limit relationships are pure functions of the carrier observations
  + canonical byte encoding and aggregate commitment require a stable ordered carrier set first
  + physical enumeration, traversal evidence, Git reconciliation, double inventory, receipt, and admission remain separable later boundaries

& [Plan] is strict and bounded
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssemblyPlan
  + [profile] exact cantor-windows-supplied-topology-inventory-assembly/0.1
  + [assembly_identity] nonzero unsigned 64-bit caller correlation syntax
  + [limits] one complete TopologyScanLimits value
  + [encoded_plan_maximum_bytes] 16384 before JSON decoding
  + unknown, missing, malformed, and type-invalid fields reject
  + current ValidateTopologyForm executes on limits
  - never: put entries, paths, counts, totals, digest, receipt, consistency, or provenance claims in the plan

& [Inputs] are completed output-only carriers
  + [root] exactly one WindowsSuppliedRootTopologyProjection by function shape
  + [directories] zero or more WindowsSuppliedDirectoryTopologyProjection values
  + [regular_files] zero or more WindowsSuppliedRegularFileTopologyProjection values
  + vectors are consumed by value after cardinality checks
  + carrier wrappers retain all lower plan, preflight, stability, content-binding, and projection lineage defined by their profiles
  - never: accept raw topology observations
  - never: accept WindowsPlatformPreflightRecord, WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair, WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding, or another lower success fragment directly
  - never: accept a deserialized carrier because none of the three carrier wrappers derives Deserialize

& [CarrierMember] is a closed output-only union
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryMember
  + [variants] Root, Directory, and RegularFile
  + each variant owns one complete corresponding carrier
  + derives Serialize but not Deserialize or Default
  + immutable access returns the projected TopologyEntryObservation and exact projection and entry-reference identities
  + no variant converts from a raw observation or lower fragment

& [EvaluationOrder] is fail closed
  + validate exact plan and current TopologyScanLimits
  + safely derive total input cardinality before internal member allocation
  + require total cardinality within maximum_entries and representable as u64
  + validate the root projected observation under current M2A rules
  + require exact RootDirectory, None path, and ordinal one
  + validate every descendant projected observation under current M2A rules
  + require directory carriers remain Directory and regular-file carriers remain RegularFile
  + require every entry volume serial equal the root volume serial exactly
  + reject duplicate projection identity
  + reject duplicate entry-reference identity
  + reject duplicate complete StrongFileIdentity
  + reject duplicate descendant relative path
  + reject duplicate observation ordinal
  + apply every structural limit with checked arithmetic
  + verify exact ancestor-directory closure
  + sort descendant carrier members by the declared structural comparator
  + require each existing descendant ordinal equal its one-based output position after the root
  + release one complete output-only assembly
  + first failure returns no partial success

& [CurrentValidation] is mandatory but bounded to this layer
  + invoke current ValidateTopologyForm on TopologyScanLimits
  + invoke current ValidateTopologyForm on every carrier topology observation
  + preserve exact nested TopologyFormFault under a distinct topology_form fault class
  + enforce carrier-specific kind again after generic validation
  + do not duplicate or weaken M2A path, kind, mode, identity, link, stream, length, digest, or ordinal rules
  - never: claim this assembly reruns lower preflight, policy, stream parsing, stability, content hashing, or carrier projection operations

& [Cardinality] is bounded before internal growth
  + compute 1 plus directory count plus regular-file count using checked usize addition
  + reject arithmetic overflow
  + convert to u64 using checked conversion
  + require total at least one and no greater than limits.maximum_entries
  + only then allocate or grow the internal member vector
  + caller allocation that already formed input vectors is outside this pure function and is not retroactively bounded

& [ProjectionIdentity] is unique caller correlation syntax
  + projection identity comes from each carrier plan getter
  + every projection identity is already nonzero under its carrier profile
  + require global uniqueness across root, directory, and regular-file carriers
  + duplicate rejects without treating projection identity as physical identity or provenance

& [EntryReferenceIdentity] is globally unique supplied correlation syntax
  + root and directory references come from their preserved stable pairs
  + regular-file reference comes from its preserved content binding stable pair
  + every reference is already nonzero under lower successful profiles
  + require global uniqueness across all members
  - never: interpret uniqueness as proof that the references came from one enumerator or actual scan

& [StrongIdentity] is exact and duplicate free within the supplied set
  + compare complete StrongFileIdentity values using exact volume_serial plus lowercase 128-bit file_id_hex equality
  + every entry volume_serial must equal the root identity volume_serial
  + every complete identity must be globally unique
  + root participates in the duplicate set
  + no partial file-ID, volume-only identity, case folding, normalization, or platform lookup is permitted
  - never: claim duplicate freedom outside the supplied member set
  - never: claim common volume serial proves root membership or physical volume correspondence

& [PathIdentity] is exact inside the supplied set
  + root relative path remains None and is not inserted into the descendant-path set
  + every descendant carrier has one Some relative path already valid under current M2A
  + require exact String uniqueness across directory and regular-file paths
  + compare case, Unicode scalars, and UTF-8 bytes exactly without normalization
  - never: claim exact supplied path uniqueness equals case-insensitive filesystem uniqueness or Git worktree truth

& [LimitChecks] apply supplied valid limits structurally
  + total member count is within maximum_entries
  + each descendant relative path UTF-8 byte length is within maximum_path_bytes
  + path depth is the count of existing slash-separated components and is within maximum_depth
  + each entry stream vector length is within maximum_streams_per_entry
  + each regular-file length is within maximum_file_bytes
  + total_file_bytes is the checked sum of regular-file length values only and is within maximum_total_bytes
  + directory and root lengths remain absent and contribute zero
  + deadline_tick is preserved in the plan but no clock is read and no deadline claim is produced

& [ParentClosure] is structural membership only
  + top-level descendants have the implicit root as parent
  + for every path with two or more components, each proper slash-joined prefix must exist exactly once in the descendant path map
  + every required prefix member must have Directory kind
  + a regular-file prefix therefore rejects
  + parent checks occur after duplicate-path rejection
  - never: claim parent closure proves no child, sibling, ignored entry, nested repository, or physical object was omitted

& [CanonicalStructuralOrder] is exact
  + root is always first and is excluded from descendant comparator input
  + split already-valid descendant paths on forward slash only
  + compare corresponding components by raw UTF-8 bytes lexicographically
  + when all shared components equal, the shorter component sequence sorts first
  + duplicate full paths reject before ordering, so kind and identity are never tiebreakers
  + sorting moves complete carrier members without rewriting any nested value
  - never: call this physical traversal order
  - never: call this Windows collation, case-insensitive order, Unicode-normalized order, or Git tree order

& [OrdinalContract] binds declarations to structural order
  + root observation ordinal is exactly one
  + first structurally ordered descendant ordinal is exactly two
  + each next descendant ordinal is exactly previous plus one through checked position conversion
  + gaps, duplicates, reversals, and otherwise mismatched ordinals reject
  + no ordinal is generated, repaired, or renumbered
  - never: claim valid ordinals prove an actual enumerator or traversal produced them

& [Output] is nonforgeable assembly success
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssembly
  + private fields are profile, plan, ordered_members, entry_count, and total_file_bytes
  + derives Serialize but not Deserialize or Default
  + immutable getters only
  + ordered_members begins with the complete root carrier and then contains complete descendant carriers in structural order
  + entry_count equals ordered_members length converted exactly to u64
  + total_file_bytes equals checked regular-file length sum
  + no public constructor, public field, mutable getter, From, or Into
  - never: expose an output that can be constructed from a raw observation vector

& [Faults] are closed, bounded, nested, and atomic
  + [codes] json, profile, assembly_identity, topology_form, cardinality, root_shape, carrier_kind, projection_identity, entry_reference, volume, strong_identity, relative_path, ordinal, limit, parent, order, arithmetic, and resource
  + exact nested TopologyFormFault exists only for topology_form
  + field is at most 64 Unicode scalars
  + message is at most 256 Unicode scalars
  + safe relative path may appear in bounded diagnostics but complete carrier or lower records do not
  + no fault contains partial assembly success

& [EvidenceGrades] remain explicit
  + [supplied] plan limits and lower records originally supplied to carrier constructors
  + [carrier_projected] every member is one completed output-only carrier
  + [current_revalidated] M2A limits and observation validation at this boundary only
  + [set_correlated] exact internal volume, uniqueness, path, parent, order, ordinal, and limit relations
  + [structurally_closed] every supplied non-top-level member has its supplied directory ancestors
  + [physically_observed] absent
  + [enumerated] absent
  + [inventory_complete] absent
  + [traversed] absent
  + [double_inventory] absent
  + [aggregate_digest_bound] absent
  + [receipted] absent
  + [admitted] absent

& [EffectBoundary] is zero
  + deterministic in-memory transformation only
  + no unsafe, Windows API, filesystem, or path-resolution API
  + no process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, or tool call
  + no Cargo dependency or lockfile change
  + no physical fixture or candidate admission builder
  + no enumeration, traversal, Git reconciliation, digest commitment, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion

